# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: libredwg-version-is-superproject-describe -- the vendored LibreDWG is stamped with CLAUTOLISP's git describe, so its build can never be cached
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: build
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-libredwg-version-is-superproject-describe

* Symptom

The LibreDWG we build and ship does not carry LibreDWG's version. Its
generated =build/src/config.h= reads, in the CI image on 2026-10-06 (libredwg
submodule at d9468ae9):

#+begin_example
#define PACKAGE_STRING "LibreDWG release-2.2.1-751-g1d02a95d"
#define PACKAGE_VERSION "release-2.2.1-751-g1d02a95d"
#+end_example

=release-2.2.1= is a CLAUTOLISP tag and =1d02a95d= a clautolisp commit.

Found while measuring ci-cache-tool-builds: a content-keyed cache of
=clautolisp/third-party/libredwg/build/= (same submodule commit, same
compiler, same flags -- a true key HIT, products touched newer than the
checkout) still recompiled all 27 C objects (197 s, against 187 s cold),
because cmake regenerated =config.h= with the new superproject commit id and
every object includes it.

* Cause

LibreDWG's CMakeLists.txt:

#+begin_src cmake
if (EXISTS ".version")
  file(READ .version NL_PACKAGE_VERSION)
else()
  find_package(Git)
  execute_process(COMMAND ${GIT_EXECUTABLE} describe --long --tags --always
                  OUTPUT_VARIABLE NL_PACKAGE_VERSION)
endif()
#+end_src

Both the =.version= test and =git describe= run in CMAKE'S WORKING DIRECTORY,
not in the source directory. =clautolisp/drawing-dwg/build-libredwg.sh= calls
=cmake -S "$lr" -B "$build"= from wherever make runs it (=clautolisp/=, via
=make -C clautolisp build-libredwg=), which is inside the SUPERPROJECT's
checkout -- so =git describe= describes clautolisp.

* Consequences

1. The version string of a shipped =libredwg= is wrong (clautolisp's
   describe at build time). To check: whether LibreDWG writes
   PACKAGE_VERSION into the files it produces (a DXF 999 comment, a DWG
   header field) -- if so, clautolisp-written drawings carry it too, and
   any golden-file test comparing them would see it change on every commit.
2. =config.h= changes on EVERY clautolisp commit, so every object is
   rebuilt every time: no build cache, and no incremental build across
   commits on the Windows runner's surviving tree, can ever help. This is
   what keeps the =libredwg= kind of =scripts/ci-build-cache.sh= unwired
   (ci-cache-tool-builds).

* Fix (proposed, not applied)

Run cmake from inside the submodule (=cd "$lr" && cmake -S . -B build ...=),
or give it =WORKING_DIRECTORY= semantics by writing a =.version= file there.
Either changes the version string of the library we ship -- from wrong to
right, but a change in a release artefact, so it is pjb's call. Then wire the
=libredwg= cache kind (see the header of =scripts/ci-build-cache.sh=) and
re-measure a hit.

* Acceptance

- =config.h= of a build of submodule commit X is byte-identical whatever the
  clautolisp commit (two commits, compare).
- A =ci-build-cache.sh restore libredwg= HIT followed by
  =make build-libraries= compiles 0 objects.

* Resolution (clautolisp 2.2.230, 2026-10-07) -- DONE

pjb's decision (2026-10-07): "we should track the new releases of libredwg
and follow 'stable' releases, so update the submodule reference and commit
(change the shipped libredwg version string)."

** Stable release: no submodule move needed

Upstream's latest STABLE release is =0.14= (GitHub release, prerelease=false,
2026-06-27; before it =0.13.4=, 2026-03-18). Every newer GitHub release
(=0.14.8590= ... =0.14.8601=) is a prerelease per-commit snapshot. The
submodule already sits at d9468ae948b8f07a08efa756c19f8916052358c0, which is
tag =0.14= (also =0.14.8363=), so the pointer is unchanged.

** What shipped

- =clautolisp/third-party/libredwg.release= records the followed release
  (=version 0.14=) and its commit.
- =clautolisp/drawing-dwg/build-libredwg.sh= writes that version to the
  submodule's =.version= (gitignored upstream, no trailing newline) and runs
  cmake from inside the submodule, so both of upstream's branches see
  LibreDWG. It FAILS when the submodule is not at the recorded commit, or
  when that commit's tags (if fetched) do not include the recorded version;
  without tags (CI's shallow submodule) or without git metadata (source
  tarball) it trusts the file. Failing, not warning: a mislabelled shipped
  library is the bug being fixed, and the message names the one-line fix.
  After configuring it checks that config.h carries the version.
  =git describe= is deliberately not the source: in a shallow clone it gives
  a bare commit id, i.e. a version that depends on how the checkout was made.
- =scripts/check-libredwg-stable-release.py=: =make check-libredwg-release=
  (offline: the recorded commit is HEAD's gitlink; part of =make
  check-release=, so of the check:release lane) and =make
  check-libredwg-stable-release= (network, manual/periodic, in no lane: is
  there a newer stable release, and at which commit). AGENTS.md "CI --
  following LibreDWG stable releases" has the procedure.
- The libredwg kind of =scripts/ci-build-cache.sh= is wired on
  =verify:packaged-dwg:linux= (now GIT_SUBMODULE_STRATEGY recursive, so the
  submodule exists when the restore runs).

** Before / after

: before  #define PACKAGE_STRING "LibreDWG release-2.2.1-781-g9fae492b"
: after   #define PACKAGE_STRING "LibreDWG 0.14"   (PACKAGE_VERSION "0.14")

** Consequence 1: do drawings carry the version?

- DWG: NO. libredwg's DWG writer adds only a constant APPID "LibreDWG"; a
  DWG written from clautolisp's empty-drawing.dxf by the old
  (release-2.2.1-...) and the new (0.14) build is byte-identical.
- DXF: YES -- out_dxf.c writes =999 / LibreDWG <PACKAGE_STRING>= as the
  first pair (JSON/GeoJSON output carry it too). clautolisp uses libredwg's
  DXF writer only for the temporary DXF of a DWG READ (clal_dwg_to_dxf),
  and its DXF reader drops 999 comments. No golden-file test in the tree
  compares libredwg-written files; the DWG suite
  (clautolisp/drawing-dwg/tests) passes 57/57.

** Acceptance

1. config.h byte-identical across clautolisp commits: built at 9fae492b
   (+ this change), then at a dummy commit on top (describe
   release-2.2.1-783-ga9fb23a8): same sha256 484646fa..., and the rebuild
   compiled 0 objects. In the CI image, two fresh clones at two clautolisp
   commits (the second with a changed version.lisp): same config.h
   (sha256 2e0b4077...).
2. =ci-build-cache.sh restore libredwg= HIT then =make build-libraries=: 0
   objects, 1 s, against 164 s / 27 objects cold (CI image, fresh clone,
   cache restored with its saved times; the whole job, incl.
   build-programs and verify-packaged-dwg.sh, left the checkout clean and
   saved the cache both times).
